{
 "id": "CMP-15",
 "name": "next-departures",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Next departures",
 "summary": "A transit departures widget the app fills: a stop name and up to three rows from host strings and numbers, each a line badge, destination, delay and minutes, which open one at a time. One layout adapts by expression to any size from 160x160 to 360x480, hides absent slots and shows an empty state.",
 "prompt": "Build a next departures widget for a transit stop: the app sends the stop, and for up to three departures the line, destination and minutes. Show a line badge, Now when it is leaving, a delay on the row, hide slots with no data, show an empty state, and tap a row to expand its details. It must fit 320x160, 160x160 and 360x480 and sizes in between.",
 "level": 3,
 "family": "CMP",
 "components": [
  "ExpandableRow",
  "Icon",
  "Departure"
 ],
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
   "layout.stack",
   "host.variables",
   "input.tap"
  ],
  "secondary": [
   "layout.weight",
   "a11y.labels",
   "a11y.state",
   "text.dynamic",
   "expr.system",
   "layout.decoration"
  ]
 },
 "use_cases": [
  "transit",
  "widget",
  "list"
 ],
 "form_factor": "widget-4x2",
 "keywords": [
  "transit",
  "departures",
  "next departures",
  "departure board",
  "bus",
  "bus times",
  "next bus",
  "train",
  "train times",
  "tram",
  "metro",
  "schedule",
  "timetable",
  "arrivals",
  "expandable",
  "expandable row",
  "expandable list",
  "accordion",
  "collapsible row",
  "collapsible list",
  "list rows",
  "rows from the app",
  "host rows",
  "host list",
  "tap to expand",
  "one open at a time",
  "line badge",
  "hidden when absent",
  "empty state",
  "adaptive widget",
  "any size"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "Rows the app fills: a fixed number of slots of exported strings and numbers, one ExpandableRow per slot through a small local component, with -1 minutes hiding a slot",
  "One layout for every size: compute how many rows fit (cap), a row height, a font size and a stack flag from windowWidth() and windowHeight(), rather than copying the rows into a stateLayout. Nothing is a hard-coded container width",
  "Keep the open row on screen in a short box: when details take the room, the shown window of slots slides so the open one stays in it",
  "Live labels: a canvas global block computes \"in 3 minutes\" and \"Delayed 4 min\" (textSubtext cut from a textMerge, then trimmed), and the row's label is a textMerge of those and the host strings",
  "In a narrow box the stack param gives the destination its own full-width line instead of squeezing it beside the minutes"
 ],
 "snippets": [
  {
   "pointer": "/components/Departure",
   "shows": "layout.stack",
   "note": "one slot: a local component around ExpandableRow, with its badge, delay, minutes and details"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/resources/variables/cap",
   "shows": "input.tap",
   "note": "how many rows fit, given the height and whether a row is open: tapping changes @open and the rows follow"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/0",
   "shows": "host.variables",
   "note": "an exported host string, with an initial value distinct from the others"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/resources/variables/stack",
   "shows": "expr.system",
   "note": "the destination gets its own line when the box is narrow or there is height to spare"
  }
 ],
